# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — Phase 12 (T012 / GAR-010 / VO-ec575c4ce42b548bfb4d)
#
# Contract: IGNORE disposable local data (regenerable build output, caches,
# reports, logs, secrets, OS/editor scratch) while RETAINING the signed
# validation manifests and fixtures that are *supported consumers* of this
# repository. A signed validation manifest (evidence/manifest.json) and the
# canonical contract/test fixtures are governed source-of-truth artifacts: a
# .gitignore change that silently swept them out of version control would break
# those consumers, violating the compatibility oracle. The `RETAINED` section at
# the bottom re-includes them with `!` negations so no disposable-data pattern
# above can ever ignore them. Enforced by tests/tooling/gitignore.test.mjs.
# =============================================================================

# --- Lisa runtime / feature state (disposable, per-run) ----------------------
.lisa/

# --- Node / npm workspace install output (regenerated by `npm ci`) -----------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.npm/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- TypeScript project-reference build output (declarations + .tsbuildinfo) --
# Disposable; regenerated by `npm run typecheck` (`tsc --build`).
.tsbuild/

# --- Bundler / compiler output (regenerable) ---------------------------------
dist/
build/
out/
lib-cov/
.turbo/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.next/
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache

# --- Test / coverage / report output (disposable, regenerated per run) -------
coverage/
.nyc_output/
test-results/
playwright-report/
playwright/.cache/
blob-report/
.vitest/
*.lcov
junit.xml

# --- Logs (disposable) -------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log

# --- Local runtime scratch / temp --------------------------------------------
tmp/
.tmp/
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock

# --- Environment / secrets — must NEVER be committed -------------------------
# (protects workspace state & secrets; the tracked example template is re-included)
.env
.env.*
# Consumer provisioning state: generated secrets, overlays, receipts (scripts/provision.sh).
.provision/
*.local

# --- OS / editor scratch (disposable) ----------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# =============================================================================
# RETAINED — supported consumers that MUST stay under version control.
# These `!` negations override the broad disposable patterns above so a signed
# validation manifest or fixture can never be accidentally ignored. Do not
# remove a line here without approved deprecation/migration/rollback evidence
# (GAR-010 / VO-ec575c4ce42b548bfb4d).
# =============================================================================

# Environment template (documents required vars; carries no secret value).
!.env.example

# Signed validation manifest — evidence/manifest.json pins every governed source
# contract + gate-evidence record by SHA-256 (tamper-evident). It is the signed
# integrity attestation the PR gate verifies; it must remain tracked.
!evidence/
!evidence/**
evidence/*.tmp
evidence/*.local.json

# Canonical contract fixtures (OpenAPI / AsyncAPI / JSON Schema source-of-truth)
# and their published specs — the supported consumer surface of the type
# generator. Fixtures are retained even though `dist/`, `build/`, `*.local`, etc.
# above are ignored.
!specs/
!specs/**

# Integration manifests (Speckit / Codex) — governed fixtures, not local scratch.
!.specify/
!.specify/**

# Test fixtures and golden files anywhere under tests/ — retained so any broad
# report/output pattern above cannot swallow a committed fixture.
!tests/**/fixtures/
!tests/**/fixtures/**
!tests/**/__fixtures__/
!tests/**/__fixtures__/**
!**/*.fixture.*
!**/*.golden.*
